<% content_for :title, "Dark Mode" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Getting Started</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Dark Mode</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    Toggles the <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">dark</code> class on <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">document.documentElement</code>. Persists preference to <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage</code> and syncs across tabs.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-8 mb-8 flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
    <button data-ui--dark-mode-target="toggle"
            data-action="click->ui--dark-mode#toggle"
            class="rounded-md bg-foreground px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-background hover:bg-foreground/90 transition-colors">
      Toggle dark mode
    </button>
    <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <span class="dark:hidden">Currently: light</span>
      <span class="hidden dark:inline">Currently: dark</span>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="w-full rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-4 shadow-sm">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">Sample card</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">This card adapts to the current theme.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-4">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#dark-mode-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="dark-mode-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_dark_mode_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Avoiding the flash of the wrong theme</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The controller only applies <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.dark</code> once Stimulus connects, which is after the stylesheet has already painted. Add this inline, before any stylesheet, in your own layout's <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;head&gt;</code> — it mirrors the controller's own resolution order and <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage</code> guarding, so the two never disagree:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Layout &lt;head&gt; — ERB, before any stylesheet</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#dark-mode-head-snippet" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="dark-mode-head-snippet" class="text-card-foreground">&lt;%= javascript_tag nonce: true do %&gt;
  (function () {
    var theme = null;
    try {
      theme = localStorage.getItem("rails_ui_kit:theme") || localStorage.getItem("theme");
    } catch (e) {}
    var prefersDark = window.matchMedia &amp;&amp; window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
    if (theme === "dark" || (theme !== "light" &amp;&amp; prefersDark)) {
      document.documentElement.classList.add("dark");
    }
  })();
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">nonce: true</code> keeps this working under a nonce-based Content-Security-Policy; it's a no-op if your app doesn't set one.
</p>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Behaviour</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground list-disc list-inside">
  <li>On <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">connect()</code>, reads <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage["rails_ui_kit:theme"]</code> (or, when that is unset, the older <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage.theme</code>); falls back to the OS <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">prefers-color-scheme</code> media query.</li>
  <li>Adds or removes the <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">dark</code> class on <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">html</code>.</li>
  <li>Listens to the <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">storage</code> event to sync across tabs.</li>
  <li>Getter: <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">this.currentTheme</code> returns <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">"dark"</code> or <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">"light"</code>.</li>
  <li>Tag the toggle button with <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-ui--dark-mode-target="toggle"</code> to get a synced <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-pressed</code> and label on connect, toggle, and cross-tab sync.</li>
  <li>That label defaults to English ("Switch to light/dark mode"). No component renders this button — you write it — so translate it by setting <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-ui--dark-mode-light-label-value</code>/<code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">-dark-label-value</code> yourself; see <%= link_to "Internationalization", i18n_path, class: "underline" %>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Tailwind setup</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The kit's tokens switch on the <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.dark</code> class, but
  Tailwind 4's own <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">dark:</code> utilities follow the OS
  preference unless you redefine the variant. <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">bin/rails generate rails_ui_kit:install</code>
  writes this line for you; if your stylesheet already defines a dark variant, the generator leaves it alone, so make sure yours matches
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.dark</code>:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">app/assets/tailwind/application.css</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#dark-mode-css" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="dark-mode-css" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_dark_mode_css) %></code></pre>
</div>
